{"tool_name":"r-mixkernel","contents":["biocontainers","oeb"],"fetched_metadata":{"biocontainers":{"name":"r-mixkernel","identifiers":["doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/btx682"],"license":"GPL (>= 2)","summary":"Kernel-based methods are powerful methods for integrating  heterogeneous types of data. mixKernel aims at providing methods to combine kernel for unsupervised exploratory analysis. Different solutions are  provided to compute a meta-kernel, in a consensus way or in a way that  best preserves the original topology of the data. mixKernel also integrates kernel PCA to visualize similarities between samples in a non linear space and from the multiple source point of view. Functions to assess and display important variables are also provided in the package. Jerome Mariette and  Nathalie Villa-Vialaneix (2017) <doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/btx682>.","home_url":"https://CRAN.R-project.org/package=mixKernel","keywords":["Breast Neoplasms","Computational Biology","Female","Humans","Unsupervised Machine Learning"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":5},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/bioconda:r-mixkernel:0.3/cmd/CRAN.R-project.org","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"bioconda","@type":"metrics","distribution":{"packages":true,"sourcecode":{}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"license":{"open_source":false,"osi":false},"publications":[],"summary":{"description":true},"website":{"bioschemas":false,"copyright":false,"https":true,"license":false,"operational":200,"redirects":[{"status":303,"url":"https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/mixKernel/index.html"}],"ssl":true,"ssl_err":null}}},{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/bioconda:r-mixkernel:0.4/cmd/CRAN.R-project.org","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"bioconda","@type":"metrics","distribution":{"packages":true,"sourcecode":{}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"license":{"open_source":false,"osi":false},"p